From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 23:19:33 -0400
Subject: test: fewer, longer browser tests where one start-up served one check

Every browser test starts and stops a whole browser, about a second on
the Mac and more under ASan, and the suite runs four times a round. In
seven fixtures most tests made one short check after that start-up.
Their checks now run as parts of fewer tests, grouped by behaviour: each
part is a lambda under its own SCOPED_TRACE with its spec comment, a
failed ASSERT ends only that part, and each part first undoes what the
parts before it changed (StartOver, KeepOneTab, CloseWhatAPartLeftOpen).
Every old check is kept.

SidebarClickTest 23 tests to 7, DarkPagesTest 17 to 6, DarkPagesButtonTest
4 to 2, SiteControlsTest 9 to 3, SidebarPanelsTest 18 to 5, SidebarSyncTest
11 to 3, ArchiveReopenTest 14 to 7 (two restart chains), SidebarRightTest
and SidebarRightRtlTest 10 to 4: 106 tests to 37. Run one at a time on the
Mac these groups took 94 s, where they took 208 s before.

Why: the owner, 2026-10-26 (the suites take too long; BACKLOG S-306).
Removable when: never; to be folded into the patches that own the tests.
